WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:04.000
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers
with Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:11.089
A caustic is a beautiful phenomenon in nature
where curved surfaces reflect or refract light,

00:00:11.089 --> 00:00:14.230
thereby concentrating it to a relatively small
area.

00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:19.140
If it's not your favorite visual phenomenon
in nature yet, which is almost impossible,

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:23.580
then you absolutely have to watch this episode.
If it is, all the better because you're gonna

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:25.269
love what's coming up now!

00:00:25.269 --> 00:00:29.689
Imagine that we have a photorealistic
rendering program that simulates the path

00:00:29.689 --> 00:00:35.989
of light rays in a scene that we put together,
and creates beautiful imagery of our caustics.

00:00:35.989 --> 00:00:41.469
However, since we, humans are pretty bad at
estimating how exactly caustics should look

00:00:41.469 --> 00:00:45.660
like, one can manipulate them to be more in
line with their artistic vision.

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:50.050
Previously, we had an episode on a technique
which made it possible to pull the caustic

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:55.390
patterns to be more visible, but this paper
offers a much more sophisticated toolset to

00:00:55.390 --> 00:00:58.600
torment these caustic patterns to our liking.

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:03.440
We can specify a target pattern that we would
like to see, and obtain a blend between what

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:08.270
would normally happen in physics and what
we imagined to appear there.

00:01:08.270 --> 00:01:12.200
It also supports animated sequences.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:17.090
Artists who use these tools are just as skilled
in their trade as the scientists who created

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:22.180
this algorithm, so I can only imagine the
miracles they will create with such a technique.

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:26.960
If you are interested in diving into photorealistic
rendering, material modeling and all that

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:31.800
cool stuff, there are completely free and
open source tools out there like Blender that

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:36.370
you can use. If you would like to get started,
check out CynicatPro's YouTube channel that

00:01:36.370 --> 00:01:50.650
has tons of really great material. Here is
a quick teaser of his channel.

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:14.800
Thanks! There is a link to his channel in
the description box, make sure to check it

00:02:14.810 --> 00:02:17.340
out and subscribe if you like what you see
there.

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:23.870
I just realized that the year has barely started
and it is already lavishing in beautiful papers.

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:27.560
Thanks for watching and for your generous
support, and I'll see you next time!

